      "body": "Found by the #624 rebuild in #653.\n\nBefore the rebuild, the surface form `Sodium glutamate\u30fbH2O` resolved to `CHEBI:64220` \u2014 the **anhydrous** `Na glutamate` record. MAPPING_SEMANTICS \u00a73 refuses that, so the rebuild correctly stops matching it, and the row is now `UNMAPPED`:\n\n```\nSodium glutamate\u30fbH2O\t4\t(chebi_id, cas_rn, kg_microbe_node_id, mim_id all empty)\tUNMAPPED\n```\n\nBut a **correct record already exists**:\n\n```\ndata/ingredients/mapped/Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.yaml\n  identifier: CHEBI:232425\n  preferred_term: Sodium glutamate monohydrate\n  mapping_status: MAPPED\n```\n\nSo the substance is curated and the name still goes nowhere \u2014 4 CultureMech occurrences that had a wrong answer now have none.\n\n**Why it misses:** an ignore-inclusive search (`rg -uu`) finds the surface form in no record at all, and the monohydrate record's synonym list carries no hydrate-notation variant:\n\n```\nsodium (2S)-2-azaniumylpentanedioate, Glutamate Sodium, Glutamate monosodium salt,\nGlutamic acid monosodium salt, Glutammato monosodico, L(+) Sodium glutamate, MSG,\nMonosodioglutammato, Natrium L-hydrogenglutamat, Natriumglutaminat,\nSodium hydrogen glutamate, sodium (2S)-2-ammoniopentanedioate\n```\n\nNothing there matches `Sodium glutamate\u30fbH2O`, and the separator is U+30FB KATAKANA MIDDLE DOT \u2014 the same non-ASCII hydrate notation that shows up elsewhere in this corpus (`(NH4)6Mo7O24\u30fb4H2O`).\n\n**Fix:** add the hydrate surface form as a synonym on `Sodium_Glutamate_Monohydrate.yaml` with a `curation_history` event. Worth checking the other `\u30fb`-separated forms for the same shape while in there \u2014 this is #251's family (hydrate notation hidden in synonyms) seen from the other side.\n\nNot a blocker for #653: the rebuild is a strict improvement over resolving a hydrate to its anhydrous parent.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BP6MDZgidgzS79c75Ykhac",
      "closed_by": null,
